 ## Background
-This method is described in "14.2 Volume Scattering Integrators" from the Physically Based Rendering (pbr-book.org) 4th edition [S1]. It is part of the VolPathIntegrator, which extends the PathIntegrator to handle participating media [S1]. The use of MIS in volumetric path tracing is a key advancement to handle the complexity of light transport in media, where both the phase function and light sources contribute to the sampling distribution [S1].
+This method is described in the context of the VolPathIntegrator in the "Physically Based Rendering" (PBRT) book, specifically in Section 14.2 "Volume Scattering Integrators" [S1]. It builds on the principles of Multiple Importance Sampling introduced in earlier chapters and extends them to the complexities of volumetric path tracing with spectral rendering.
 
